        content: `At-will employment is the default in all US states except Montana. Either party may terminate the relationship at any time, for any reason (or no reason), with or without notice. However, numerous exceptions limit at-will doctrine: (1) Public policy exception - cannot fire for refusing illegal acts, exercising legal rights, or performing public duties; (2) Implied contract exception - employee handbooks or employer statements may create contractual protections; (3) Implied covenant of good faith - minority of states recognize; (4) Statutory exceptions - anti-discrimination laws, whistleblower protection, WARN Act, etc.`,
